IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aoma-majority`

-- Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA), ss 4 and 5 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_age-of-majority-act-1972_baseline.py). Expected results were
-- written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe): Chloe, born 14 March 2003, turns 18 on
-- 14 March 2021 (c025). The commencing day is not in the deposit: 1 January 1973 below is an ASSUMED placeholder, used
-- only to exercise s 4(2) and s 5(1)(b); any commencing day before 2021 gives Chloe the same answers. The other people
-- are the encoder's illustrations, not scenario events.

§ `s 4 -- the moment I reach an age`

-- c025: Chloe reaches 18 at the very start of 14 March 2021, and 21 at the start of 14 March 2024.
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 14 3 2003) 18 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 14 3 2003) 21 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2024))
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 29 2 2004) 18 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not fixed by the Act: I was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`at the very start of` (Date 29 2 2020))
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 1 6 1950) 18 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When do I reach this age` (Date 1 1 1955) 18 (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`at the very start of` (Date 1 1 1973))

§ `s 5(1) -- when I come of full age`

-- c025: Chloe comes of full age under s 5(1)(a) at the start of her 18th birthday.
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`on attaining 18, at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 1 1 1955) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`on attaining 18, at the very start of` (Date 1 1 1973))
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 1 6 1953) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`on the commencing day` (Date 1 1 1973))
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 2 1 1952) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS (`on the commencing day` (Date 1 1 1973))
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 1 1 1952) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 1 6 1950) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age` (Date 29 2 2004) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`

-- c025: the day before, Chloe is not of full age; on the day, she is.
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 13 3 2021) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 14 3 2021) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 1 6 1953) (Date 31 12 1972) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 1 6 1953) (Date 1 1 1973) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 1 6 1950) (Date 20 10 2026) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on this day` (Date 29 2 2004) (Date 1 3 2022) (Date 1 1 1973) EQUALS `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`

§ `s 5(2), (3), (5), (7) -- how the word is read`

#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `minor` `a WA enactment` FALSE EQUALS `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `sui juris` `a WA enactment` FALSE EQUALS `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `full age` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` FALSE EQUALS `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `infant` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` TRUE EQUALS `as that law defines it or as its contrary intention shows`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `an age expressed in years` `a WA enactment` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: the age in years stands as written (s 5(3))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `an age expressed in years` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: the age in years stands as written (s 5(3))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `adult` `a written instrument made before the commencing day` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: an instrument made before the commencing day (s 5(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `minority` `a will made before the commencing day, confirmed by a codicil on or after it` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: a will made before the commencing day is not remade by a later codicil (s 5(2)(b), (5))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `minor` `a Commonwealth law, another State's law, or a document under one` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: this Act reaches only the laws of the State (ss 3, 5(1))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `adult` `an industrial award, order, determination or agreement` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `infant` `an apprenticeship instrument made under an enactment on wages and conditions` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `How is this expression read` `full age` `a provision of an enactment on conditions of employment` FALSE EQUALS `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`

§ `s 5(4) -- what turning 18 does not cure`

#ASSERT `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `my age` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `my age` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `insanity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `mental infirmity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `another factor distinct from age` TRUE

